    {
        "content": "<p>SilverMira opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14376\">PR #14376</a> from <code>SilverMira:main</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>closes: issue #14366</p>\n<p>Through some trait and lifetime magic, it is possible to effectively specify a <code>Send</code> bound on the unnamed <code>Future</code> returned by <code>AsyncFnOnce</code> on stable. </p>\n<p>This commit uses said magic and changes <code>AccessorTask</code> from a manually implemented trait into an async closure returning a <code>Future</code> that is <code>Send</code>. Users can now pass <code>async move |accessor| { ... }</code>  into <code>Accessor::spawn</code> and friends directly, skipping boilerplate of creating a struct and implementing <code>AccessorTask</code> manually.</p>\n<p>Additionally, it is no longer intended for users to manually implement <code>AccessorTask</code>, as implementing the trait now requires Self to also implement <code>AsyncFnOnce</code>, which is unstable.</p>\n<p>All occurrences that manually implement <code>AccessorTask</code> within the repo is updated to just use an async closure.</p>\n<p>I have verified that rustc is happy with <code>cargo check -p wasmtime-wasi-tls</code> as recommended in #14366, in both the nightly trait solver and stable trait solver via <code>RUSTFLAGS=-Znext-solver=coherence</code>.</p>\n<p>This is a breaking change of course.<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 626026985,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1790083573
